 "The fundamentals point clearly Republican: an R+7 open seat, a favorable national environment, and Strada's overwhelming financial advantage after a hard-fought primary recount win. A single Democratic-sponsored July poll showing a tie is the lone counterpoint, but it is old and low-weight, so the forecast stays near the combined fundamentals and rating consensus at roughly R+8.", "watch": "Any fresh independent polling showing Pericola competitive, or signs the divisive GOP primary left Strada weakened among swing voters, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 57 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Daniel Webster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Republicans are favored to hold this open Central Florida seat, where Daniel Webster's retirement leaves the district without an incumbent. Joe Strada emerged from a recount-marred GOP primary and enters the general election with a commanding financial position, having raised over $5 million to Democrat James Pericola's roughly $120,000. The district's R+7 lean and a national environment favoring Republicans reinforce that advantage.\n\nEvery major race rater places the seat on the Republican side of the ledger, and prediction markets price a Democratic win at only about 12 percent. A July poll sponsored by a Democratic-leaning firm showed a 42-42 tie, but it is the only public survey and is now two months old. Absent new evidence of a competitive race, this remains Likely Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -7.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1312, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1199, "margin": -8.0}]}